  "id": "false-rejection",
  "term": "false rejection",
  "definition": "False rejection is a misidentification error in which two samples from the same individual are not recognized as belonging to that individual. In capture-mark-recapture work, this can distort estimated survival and detection measures and may also affect other estimates when sample size is low.",
